From: OpenHarmony PC Developer Community <dev@openharmony.org>
Date: 2026-03-27
Subject: [PATCH] pylifecycle.c: dup() fd validation for HarmonyOS

Add __OHOS__ to fd validation guard.

Applies to: CPython 3.9.0
---
--- a/Python/pylifecycle.c	2020-10-05 23:07:58.000000000 +0800
+++ b/Python/pylifecycle.c	2026-03-26 21:03:30.935171407 +0800
@@ -1754,7 +1754,7 @@
 
    Only use dup() on platforms where dup() is enough to detect invalid FD in
    corner cases: on Linux and Windows (bpo-32849). */
-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(MS_WINDOWS)
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__OHOS__) || defined(MS_WINDOWS)
     if (fd < 0) {
         return 0;
     }
